### 3.2. Retention Metrics (FY 2024)

Retention metrics are critical indicators of product-market fit and customer success effectiveness. It is important to note the distinction between the four key metrics, which measure different aspects of customer loyalty and revenue stability. (For a deeper dive into churn drivers, see the dedicated report **SALES-003: Churn Analysis**).

| Metric | Value | Definition |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Logo Retention Rate** | **87%** | Percentage of customers who renewed their contract (excluding revenue expansion/contraction). |
| **Customer Retention Rate (by count)** | **91%** | Percentage of customers retained from the start of the period. |
| **Gross Revenue Retention (GRR)** | **94%** | Percentage of recurring revenue retained from the existing customer base (excluding expansion revenue). |
| **Net Revenue Retention (NRR)** | **118%** | Percentage of recurring revenue retained from the existing customer base (including expansion revenue). |

The NRR of **118%** is a key highlight, demonstrating that the revenue gained from existing customers through upsells and cross-sells significantly outpaced the revenue lost to churn and down-sells.

